          "blocks": {
            "q1": {
              "type": "sp-faq-row",
              "name": "How do I choose the right product?",
              "settings": {
                "question": "How do I choose the right product?",
                "answer": "<p>Start from the eight product families above and narrow by what you are probing and how you are holding it — manipulators and probe arms position the contact, chucks and holders hold the device under test, and pumps and compressors supply them. If you are not sure, <a href=\"/pages/contact\">tell us about your application</a> and we will point you at the right family.</p>"
              }
            },
            "q2": {
              "type": "sp-faq-row",
              "name": "How do configurations and variants work?",
              "settings": {
                "question": "How do configurations and variants work?",
                "answer": "<p>Each family is offered in a number of configurations, listed on that family's page as variants — 57 across the eight families. A configuration fixes the things that have to match your station, such as series, base type, orientation or size.</p>"
              }
            },
            "q3": {
              "type": "sp-faq-row",
              "name": "How do I know which probe arm fits my manipulator?",
              "settings": {
                "question": "How do I know which probe arm fits my manipulator?",
                "answer": "<p>Coaxial and triaxial arms are used for DC and low-frequency work. High frequency arms fit the MA-9000, MA-9100 and MA-8500 manipulators and come in West/East and North/South orientations, and they accept industry-standard probes from Cascade and GGB.</p>"
              }
            },
            "q4": {
              "type": "sp-faq-row",
              "name": "Can I buy individual components, or do I need a complete assembly?",
              "settings": {
                "question": "Can I buy individual components, or do I need a complete assembly?",
                "answer": "<p>Components are sold individually. These are the same parts SemiProbe specifies into its own probe systems, so a single manipulator, arm, chuck or box of tips can be ordered on its own.</p>"
              }
            },
            "q5": {
              "type": "sp-faq-row",
              "name": "Will these work with a probe station from another manufacturer?",
              "settings": {
                "question": "Will these work with a probe station from another manufacturer?",
                "answer": "<p>Often, yes. The PS4L adaptive architecture is interchangeable, configurable and field-upgradable, and the accessory range follows the same principle. <a href=\"/pages/contact\">Send us the station you are working with</a> and we will confirm the fit before you order.</p>"
              }
            },
            "q6": {
              "type": "sp-faq-row",
              "name": "Where can I find detailed specifications?",
              "settings": {
                "question": "Where can I find detailed specifications?",
                "answer": "<p>Specifications are on each product page, under the family it belongs to. For anything not published there, including drawings and tolerances, <a href=\"/pages/contact\">ask us</a> and we will send it.</p>"
              }
            },
            "q7": {
              "type": "sp-faq-row",
              "name": "What if I need a configuration that isn't listed?",
              "settings": {
                "question": "What if I need a configuration that isn't listed?",
                "answer": "<p>Unlisted configurations may still be built. Standardized and customized probe arms, chucks and manipulators are all made to order, so <a href=\"/pages/contact\">describe what you need</a> and we will tell you whether it can be done.</p>"
              }
            }
          },
